Description: DANOS vrfaware-snmp-reqs-traps-support.patch, rebased onto net-snmp 5.9.5.2
 Ported to 5.9: sockets are bound to the VRF through upstream's
 <address>@<iface>:<port> support. DANOS's [<address>:]<port>:<vrf> syntax
 (written by vyatta-service-snmp) is mapped onto it in netsnmp_parse_ep_str,
 and TCP and UDP/IPv6 client sockets are bound as upstream already does for
 UDP/IPv4. Trap sink contexts (-n <context>) are kept.
Origin: vendor, https://github.com/danos/net-snmp debian/patches

